{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A local caller can read hidden verification artifacts and private run data without credentials when token enforcement is enabled."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"With a trusted local proxy configured, a local process can impersonate it and create or steer runs without authentication."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unauthenticated local process can revoke all owner sessions and repeatedly prevent the owner from maintaining access."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A land check resumed during startup can receive a sandbox profile that allows it to read the subsequently published owner token."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An accidental second daemon start replaces the running daemon's token and causes authenticated coordination and deploy requests to fail."},{"id":"F6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Enabling enforcement leaves the local sign-in page redirecting an unsigned-in owner away, preventing normal authenticated UI actions."},{"id":"F7","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Authentication failures lose their explanatory message or are not reported by follow, leaving the operator with inadequate diagnostics."}]}